From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:36:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/25] Let ModelOpt mixed precision quantize GLM KDA and MLA
 projections

Source: knapcio/GLM-5.3-Flash-4x-DGX-Spark-TP4, overlay/glm5next_kda.py
and overlay/glm5next_model.py (stop stripping quant_config from KDA and
MLA), commit 770d115, MIT License, author knapcio. Re-implemented and
narrowed to ModelOpt MIXED_PRECISION; knapcio's FP8_BLOCK algo and loader
filter are not ported because v0.31.0 already loads FP8_PB_WO and MXFP8.

Upstream status: not upstream. vLLM main (0f112d180) still builds the
GLM-5.3-Flash KDA projections and MLA (with its indexer wq_b) with
quant_config=None.

What/why: the released GLM-5.3-Flash checkpoints keep the KDA, MLA and
indexer projections in BF16. Glm5NextLinearAttention and the MLA layer
therefore drop the global quant config, so NVFP4 or FP8 never reach
them. That also blocks a ModelOpt MIXED_PRECISION checkpoint that stores
those projections as FP8_PB_WO (128x128 block FP8) or MXFP8.
Both sites now pass the config through only when it is
ModelOptMixedPrecisionConfig (the indexer's wq_b inherits MLA's config).
That config maps every layer missing from quantized_layers to
UnquantizedLinearMethod, so unlisted projections (kv_b_proj, f_b/g_b,
wk_weights_proj) stay BF16. Every other config still gets None, so
existing checkpoints are unaffected. MLAAttention
gets no KV-cache method from the mixed config (it is not an Attention
subclass), the same as before.

Claimed gain and config: the lossless8 checkpoint
(tools/lossless8.py on nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4) re-encodes 264
projection groups on their native grids. Per-rank decode weight bytes
per token drop from 5.23 to 3.52 GiB at TP=4 and from 9.91 to 6.67 GiB
at TP=2 (header-only model, batch 1). knapcio README (2026-09-28)
measured step -7.5 ms and 0.25% output error for the same scheme on 4x
DGX Spark TP=4 with W8A16 Marlin. Serve with --linear-backend marlin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/models/glm5next/common/kda.py   | 10 ++++++++--
 vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py |  9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/glm5next/common/kda.py b/vllm/models/glm5next/common/kda.py
index 436b9685c..cc7b1c693 100644
--- a/vllm/models/glm5next/common/kda.py
+++ b/vllm/models/glm5next/common/kda.py
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@ from vllm.model_executor.layers.mamba.ops.gather_initial_states import (
     gather_initial_states,
 )
 from vllm.model_executor.layers.mamba.ops.scatter_states import scatter_states
+from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.modelopt import (
+    ModelOptMixedPrecisionConfig,
+)
 from vllm.model_executor.model_loader.weight_utils import sharded_weight_loader
 from vllm.model_executor.utils import (
     maybe_disable_graph_partition,
@@ -185,10 +188,13 @@ class Glm5NextLinearAttention(GatedDeltaNetAttention):
         vllm_config: VllmConfig,
         prefix: str = "",
     ) -> None:
-        # KDA projections remain BF16 because fp8 checkpoints omit their scales.
+        # KDA projections remain BF16 because fp8 checkpoints omit their scales,
+        # unless a ModelOpt MIXED_PRECISION config lists them in quantized_layers
+        # (unlisted layers stay unquantized there).
         saved_quant_config = vllm_config.quant_config
         try:
-            vllm_config.quant_config = None
+            if not isinstance(saved_quant_config, ModelOptMixedPrecisionConfig):
+                vllm_config.quant_config = None
             super().__init__(config, vllm_config, prefix)
         finally:
             vllm_config.quant_config = saved_quant_config
diff --git a/vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py b/vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py
index d5274cc7b..66c5a44aa 100644
--- a/vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py
+++ b/vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py
@@ -42,6 +42,9 @@ from vllm.model_executor.layers.mhc import (
     hc_expand,
 )
 from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization import QuantizationConfig
+from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.modelopt import (
+    ModelOptMixedPrecisionConfig,
+)
 from vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.utils.quant_utils import (
     GroupShape,
     scaled_dequantize,
@@ -329,7 +332,11 @@ class Glm5NextDecoderLayer(nn.Module):
                 kv_lora_rank=config.kv_lora_rank,
                 max_position_embeddings=config.max_position_embeddings,
                 cache_config=cache_config,
-                quant_config=None,  # MLA projections are BF16 in checkpoint
+                # MLA projections are BF16 in released checkpoints; a ModelOpt
+                # MIXED_PRECISION config quantizes only what it lists.
+                quant_config=quant_config
+                if isinstance(quant_config, ModelOptMixedPrecisionConfig)
+                else None,
                 prefix=f"{prefix}.self_attn",
                 topk_indices_buffer=topk_indices_buffer,
                 skip_rope=config.mla_nope,
